From: SenkOS
Subject: [PATCH] super standby: let the PMIC cut the SoC's power

When BL31 asks for it (params->poweroff), save the words PHY training overwrites to DRAM
(params->save_addr) and sum BL31's 256 KiB, leave SPL the resume entry, DRAM config, that
buffer and the sum in the RTC, and set the AXP717's auto sleep bit; BL31 armed the rest.
Before that, as the stock standby program does: AHB and the R_PRCM buses to the internal
RC oscillator, the 24 MHz oscillator to the hardware's clock request, so it stops with the
SoC. Waking up is a cold boot, SPL brings DRAM back and jumps to the warm entry. If the
power is still on 2-3 s later (RTC seconds: the arch timer may have stopped with the
oscillator), the stub puts the clocks back, clears the handshake and sleeps in WFI as before.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 0aeec2f..05bf6ab 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ else
   $(error suspend-stub: no known DRAM type in $(DEFCONFIG))
 endif
 
-OBJS := src/start.o src/main.o src/lib.o src/clock.o src/dram_sr.o \
+OBJS := src/start.o src/main.o src/lib.o src/clock.o src/dram_sr.o src/pmic.o \
